# PROGRAM: dv/auto_dv/stim/gen_directed/gen_irq_ack_directed.S, built by
#   gen_program.py --directed <that file> --seed 1 --out <dir> --gcc-opts=-I<root>/dv/auto_dv/tests/gen_programs
#   image 144 words, crc32 0x073dcaa4, entry 0x80000080, tohost 0x800002a0. Every cause vectors to one
#   handler that reads mcause, reports the lower cause to GEN_MM_EOT_ADDR and stores THAT cause to
#   GEN_MM_IRQ_ACK_ADDR, then mrets.
#
# WHICH LINE THE ACK BELONGS TO: every run below raises mask 0x00044 in ONE IRQ_SET under UNTIL_ACK:
#   fast[3] (driver line 6, mie bit and mcause lower cause 19) and external (driver line 2, cause 11).
#   Controller priority takes fast[3] first (gen_irq_rank: a fast id outranks external), so the
#   acknowledgement belongs to CAUSE 19, LINE 6; the line that must survive it and be taken in its own
#   entry is EXTERNAL, CAUSE 11, LINE 2. The failing runs below are exactly the runs where cause 11
#   never arrives.
#
# CLAIM: an acknowledgement releases the one line whose cause it names. NOT CLAIMED HERE: any
#   behaviour of a long storm run (the two storm runs at the end are one short window), and the
#   gen_test_irq_basic program's own ack ordering, which is the Test Writer's.
#
